  "install": [
   "sudo apt-get update -q && sudo apt-get install -y -q gdal-bin libgdal-dev",
   "pip install --quiet \"GDAL==$(gdal-config --version)\" pyproj python-dateutil scikit-image matplotlib",
   "git init -q \"$RUNNER_TEMP/acolite\" && git -C \"$RUNNER_TEMP/acolite\" fetch -q --depth 1 https://github.com/acolite/acolite.git ca477dd91dfb5f8eb77333824b38cb0bcce5e083 && git -C \"$RUNNER_TEMP/acolite\" checkout -q FETCH_HEAD",
   "export S2FDI_ACOLITE_DIR=\"$RUNNER_TEMP/acolite\"   # (the adapter clones the same commit itself if unset)",
   "python3 -c \"from osgeo import gdal; assert gdal.GetDriverByName('JP2OpenJPEG')\""
  ],
  "install_note": "how the probe got ACOLITE: `git clone --depth 1 https://github.com/acolite/acolite.git` (colocation_probe.acolite_dir) into the sandbox, which already had GDAL 3.8.4 Python bindings (pip-built against Ubuntu 24.04's libgdal-dev, JP2OpenJPEG driver present), netCDF4, pyproj, scipy, scikit-image, matplotlib. ACOLITE's LUTs (~760 MB on disk for S2A+S2B) download on first use from raw.githubusercontent.com/acolite/acolite_luts \u2014 about 40 s once per job (an actions/cache of acolite/data/LUT would save it).",
